{"chunk_id": "0a287fb13868", "text": "This section depicts the ferocity of Bhishma on the battlefield and the strategic effort to bring him down. Bhishma is portrayed like a blazing fire consuming armies, his arrows devastating thousands of warriors from many kingdoms. Even massive formations collapse before him, and soldiers fear approaching him. Sikhandin advances and wounds Bhishma, but Bhishma refuses to strike back because he remembers Sikhandin\u2019s former femininity. Arjuna urges Sikhandin to press the attack, knowing Bhishma will not fight him fully. Meanwhile Dussasana fights fiercely to shield the grandsire and momentarily holds off the Pandavas until Arjuna defeats him and advances. Duryodhana rallies his troops, proclaiming Bhishma invincible and urging a mass assault on Arjuna. The passage highlights Bhishma\u2019s near-mythic power and the crucial tactic of using Sikhandin to neutralize him.\nBhishma devastates the Pandava forces while refusing to strike Sikhandin, as Arjuna advances under heavy opposition urged by Duryodhana.\nThemes: Bhishma\u2019s battlefield supremacy, Sikhandin and gender vow, Arjuna vs Bhishma setup, Kaurava morale and command, heroic slaughter in war", "vector": [-0.0205856803804636, -0.004068090580403805, 0.0008200847078114748, 0.029239190742373466, -0.0035507611464709044, 0.02843296341598034, -0.03558151423931122, -0.014498661272227764, -0.01608424261212349, -0.034990280866622925, 0.01633954793214798, 0.006100456230342388, 0.006960432510823011, 0.010783295147120953, 0.006953713949769735, -0.0010195421054959297, 0.047029949724674225, 0.01111250463873148, 0.024025585502386093, -0.023918088525533676, -0.018529798835515976, 0.0008133661467581987, 0.003960593603551388, 0.02452275902032852, -0.03130850940942764, 0.04321380332112312, 0.014834589324891567, -0.021754710003733635, -0.0031039766035974026, 0.0014218160649761558, -0.010884073562920094, -0.0021734554320573807, -0.0008524178410880268, 0.002806680044159293, -0.0366296097636